{"availability":"available","full":"clidey/whodb","name":"whodb","description":"Where data access meets operational intelligence","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":5032,"forks":242,"created":"2024-06-11T10:10:59Z","updated":"2026-10-04T04:38:29Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://whodb.com","topics":["ai-agent","data-catalog","data-governance","data-integration","data-lineage","data-pipeline","data-platform","database-management","er-diagram","internal-tools","mcp-server","model-context-protocol","mysql","oracle","postgresql","self-hosted","sql-editor","sqlserver","text-to-sql","visual-query-builder"],"demo":"https://demo.whodb.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:12.199Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:12.199Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:18:12.199Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:18:12.199Z","stars":5032,"forks":242}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Quick start · Documentation · Live demo · Community","WhoDB gives you one place to explore your databases, edit data, run queries, and understand how a schema fits together. It runs in the browser, is easy to self-host, and is available as a desktop app or terminal CLI too.","Use it when you want to inspect a local database, help a teammate explore unfamiliar data, or work without installing a heavyweight database client. AI features are optional: connect Ollama, OpenAI, Anthropic, LM Studio, or another OpenAI-compatible provider if you want to ask questions in plain English."],"features":["Browse and edit data in a spreadsheet-style grid with sorting, filtering, pagination, and inline editing.","Understand a schema visually with an interactive graph of tables and relationships.","Work through queries in a scratchpad with multiple cells, autocomplete, history, and results kept alongside each query.","Move data in and out with imports, exports, and mock-data generation for development and testing.","Ask questions in plain English using a local or hosted AI provider that you choose."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"af171b5a89df8b35c8cbef7a72c529c00503c8ff23fb3a3bd99fb3236c5fc464","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:10.942Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:10.942Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Quick start · Documentation · Live demo · Community","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"It runs in the browser, is easy to self-host, and is available as a desktop app or terminal CLI too.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"To keep encrypted login sessions when the container is replaced, first generate a key and save it somewhere secure:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"optional","text":"It is free to self-host and is the best place to start if you want to explore and work with databases.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"af171b5a89df8b35c8cbef7a72c529c00503c8ff23fb3a3bd99fb3236c5fc464","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:10.943Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T04:38:29Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clidey/whodb/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:52:10.944Z","hash":"af171b5a89df8b35c8cbef7a72c529c00503c8ff23fb3a3bd99fb3236c5fc464","originalBytes":10985,"storedBytes":10985,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["whodb","data","docker","start","bash","provider","ollama","run","backend","cli","connection","mcp","anthropic","available","database","key","local","openai","see","community","documentation","edit","guide","open","providers","server","studio","support","terminal"